-- title:
--   Good Hecke operators suffice on the primitive packet of J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number, $\varepsilon$ a Dirichlet character modulo $M$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and $g$ a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ which is primitive for $\varepsilon$ in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm`](def/CuspForm_PrimitiveFormGamma1.html#L38): its $q$-coefficients satisfy $a_1(g)=1$, the relation $a_{pn}(g)+\varepsilon(p)\,p\,[p\mid n]\,a_{n/p}(g)=a_p(g)a_n(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M$ and all $n$, multiplicativity $a_{\ell n}(g)=a_\ell(g)a_n(g)$ for primes $\ell\mid M$, nebentypus $\varepsilon$, and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ does the eigenpacket $(a_n(g))_n$, $(\varepsilon(n))_n$ occur at level $M'$. Assume further the Hecke–diamond inputs [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) and the pairwise commutation [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) of the generators, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals. Give $J_1(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) over $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}=\mathbb{Z}[X_{\ell},X_d]$, the polynomial ring on primes and naturals. Then for every $t$ in this ring there are $s,u$ in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by the $\mathrm{heckeGenOne}\,\ell$ and $\mathrm{diamondGen}\,\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, such that the evaluation of $s$ at $X_\ell\mapsto a_\ell(g)\varepsilon(\ell)^{-1}$, $X_d\mapsto\varepsilon(d)^{-1}$ is non-zero and $(st)\cdot x=u\cdot x$ for all $x\in J_1(M)$.
--
--   This is the form taken here by strong multiplicity one together with newform theory: on the component of $J_1(M)$ cut out by the packet of a primitive $g$, every Hecke–diamond operator — including those at primes dividing $M$ or in the excluded set $S$ — is, after multiplication by an element not annihilating that packet, represented by an operator built from the good generators $T_\ell$, $\langle\ell\rangle$ with $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$. It is used in the construction of the $g$-part of the Tate module of $J_1(M)$, via [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.iInf_ker_hecke_sub_ne_bot_and_inf_span_eq_bot_tateModule_jOne`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.iInf_ker_hecke_sub_ne_bot_and_inf_span_eq_bot_tateModule_jOne).
